Build the queue manager core library that other components use. This is the data layer — no DCL commands yet.

## Scope
A C library (src/vmsqueue/ or within libvms) that manages queue state.

### Data model:
```c
struct vms_queue {
    char name[32];          // SYS$BATCH, SYS$PRINT, user-defined
    uint8_t type;           // BATCH=1, PRINT=2, GENERIC=3
    uint8_t status;         // STARTED=1, STOPPED=2, PAUSED=3
    uint32_t entry_count;
    uint32_t next_entry_id;
};

struct vms_queue_entry {
    uint32_t entry_id;      // VMS job number
    char queue_name[32];
    char job_name[256];     // filename or procedure name
    char username[64];
    uint8_t status;         // PENDING=1, EXECUTING=2, HOLDING=3, COMPLETED=4
    uint64_t submit_time;   // VMS binary time
    uint64_t start_time;
    uint8_t priority;
};
```

### API:
```c
int vmsq_init(const char *db_path);           // Open/create QMAN$MASTER.DAT
int vmsq_create_queue(const char *name, int type);
int vmsq_delete_queue(const char *name);
int vmsq_submit(const char *queue, const char *job, const char *user, uint32_t *entry_id);
int vmsq_show_queue(const char *queue, struct vms_queue *info);
int vmsq_show_entries(const char *queue, struct vms_queue_entry *entries, int max, int *count);
int vmsq_show_entry(uint32_t entry_id, struct vms_queue_entry *entry);
int vmsq_delete_entry(uint32_t entry_id);
int vmsq_hold_entry(uint32_t entry_id);
int vmsq_release_entry(uint32_t entry_id);
int vmsq_update_status(uint32_t entry_id, uint8_t new_status);
void vmsq_close(void);
```

### Storage format (QMAN$MASTER.DAT):
- Binary file with fixed-size records
- Header: magic, version, queue count, entry count
- Queue table: array of vms_queue structs
- Entry table: array of vms_queue_entry structs
- Simple append + rewrite model (no complex B-tree)

### Boot initialization:
- ovmx_init creates default queues if QMAN$MASTER.DAT is empty:
  - SYS$BATCH (batch queue, started)
  - SYS$PRINT (print queue, started)

